WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.490
Syrian Kurds here, in Qamishli, northeastern
Syria are angry.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:09.370
In December, Donald Trump surprised everyone
by annonucing that the US would pull out of

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.670
Syria - and quickly.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:17.350
That could leave the Kurds vulnerable to attacks
from Turkey which sees some of them as terrorists.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:22.070
The Kurds have been fighting tooth and nail
against Islamic State alongside US troops.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:24.539
its been a costly fight.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:31.439
The Kurds fear being abandoned by a US withdrawal
and so too do many of the US's allies in the

00:00:31.439 --> 00:00:32.950
region.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.410
Enter John Bolton...

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.420
US National Security Advisor.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:41.930
He's jetting around the Middle East clarifying
confusion, putting out the fire that Trump

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:42.930
started.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:46.920
His message: the US isn't simply packing up
and leaving.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.059
In December, Trump told the Pentagon to prepare
to leave Syria within a 100 days.

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:54.430
Now, he's changed his mind:
We are pulling back in Syria.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.230
We`re going to be removing our troops.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:02.559
I never said we`re doing it that quickly
Bolton, recently in Israel, also says that

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:04.750
the US's withdrawal is conditional.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:10.970
We're gonna to be discussing the president's
decision to withdraw but to do so from northeast

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:18.390
Syria in a way that makes sure that ISIS (Islamic
State group) is defeated and is not able to

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:23.759
revive itself
He's in Ankara to assure Turkey that the US

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:26.259
WILL leave... but bit by bit.

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:29.509
That chimes with Reccep Tayyip Erdogan, Turkey's
President.

00:01:29.509 --> 00:01:34.220
Turkey sees itself as the dominant regional
power writing in the New York Times this week,

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:45.350
he said he agreed

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:57.369
that the US SHOULD withdraw... but, slowly.

00:01:57.369 --> 00:02:14.680
Bolton has a big challenge in Ankara: his
OTHER condition for a

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:38.160
US withdrawal is

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:55.319
that 
Turkey PROMISES not to attack

00:02:55.319 --> 00:03:05.349
the US's allies, the Kurds.

00:03:05.349 --> 00:03:36.819
For Turkey, which has a long-standing and
bloody fued with

00:03:36.819 --> 00:04:13.340
the Kurds, that 
will

00:04:13.340 --> 00:05:17.240
be hard

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:29.129
to swallow.

